\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TSuperIncorp
\item[* relevant examples:] the most long $\rightarrow$  the longest
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] TC\_ComparIncorp
\item[* date of creation:] 17-APR-1989
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] English TADJmostTOst
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] morphological incorporation of the superlative
expression `most'
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) It is assumed 
that superdeixis and thanascompl of the QP are indeed default. \\
If moreComp is 
in the set of possible compformations, but not as the only member, both the 
current rule and the default rule apply.\\
Finally, it is assumed that the present rule and the previous one (for 
comparative formation) are mutually exclusive. Note that they are called only
after AdjClauseFormation, and not after any of the other clause formation rules
(see the control expression)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
mu2 for all kinds of arguments and modifiers (not degreemodifiers),
mu3 for modifiers of {\em the most}
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
