TADJmostNOTTOst + TADJNOestNOmost
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] This rule functions as a default rule.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) Note that 
this ruled is called only
after AdjClauseFormation, and not after any of the other clause formation rules
(see the control expression). If it were decided that the transformation 
class must be applied irrespective of the kind of clause, the rule must be 
adapted to refer to the VERBP only, and have as matchcondition that there is 
no predrel/ADJP in it with a head/ADJ etc.
